# Pairs with NoKeyLost. Reproduces current production (#4452) from the resize
# side: the resize starts while a split is in flight. Writes acknowledged on
# the split target T/s2 after the split commits are never mirrored to R, and
# the flip routes k2 to R/s1, which does not hold them.
#
# DEADLOCK: off for the same reason as UniqueOwnerSplitDuringResize.
MODULE: NoKeyLostResizeDuringSplit
TARGET: NoKeyLost
CLASS: Invariant
DEADLOCK: off
SUMMARY: a resize starts with a split in flight, so writes on the split target are lost at the flip
PERTURBS: ResizeBegin

--- FIND
    /\ rs # "migrating"
    /\ sp \in {"idle", "done"}
    /\ rz' = "snap"
--- REPLACE
    /\ rs # "migrating"
\* MUTATION: no interlock with an in-flight split.
    /\ rz' = "snap"
--- END